  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, in an 80 person instance, VRAM usage tends to hover around the 16gb mark (or a bit higher if the user does not know to turn off SteamVR Home)\n\nGPUs with 12/16gb of VRAM are likely to become FAR more commonplace with the next generation of hardware.\n\nThis means that in large events, users of 16gb cards are usually capable of showing 60 or 70 users without issue. Users of 12gb cards may be able to show 40 or 50 without issue.\n\nHowever, the current slider only goes up to 30, which forces people to hide a whopping 50 people -- most of the instance -- when they may only really need to cut out 5-20 of them.\n\nThis has a large impact on the event experience and the solution is to slightly change an option slider, so it'd be much appreciated if you could remove the restriction on this feature.",
